{"surah": 102, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "أَلْهَىٰكُمُ ٱلتَّكَاثُرُ ", "translation": "Competition in [worldly] increase diverts you", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَلْهَىٰكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkٰàَhْlَaʾ", "root": "لهو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلتَّكَاثُرُ", "translit": "ُrُhtāَkَّtlٱ", "root": "كثر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "حَتَّىٰ زُرْتُمُ ٱلْمَقَابِرَ ", "translation": "Until you visit the graveyards.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "زُرْتُمُ", "translit": "ُmُtْrُz", "root": "زور"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمَقَابِرَ", "translit": "َrِbāَqَmْlٱ", "root": "قبر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "كَلَّا سَوْفَ تَعْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "No! You are going to know.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَلَّا", "translit": "āَّlَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "سَوْفَ", "translit": "َfْwَs", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَt", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "ثُمَّ كَلَّا سَوْفَ تَعْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "Then, no! You are going to know.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَلَّا", "translit": "āَّlَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "سَوْفَ", "translit": "َfْwَs", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَt", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "كَلَّا لَوْ تَعْلَمُونَ عِلْمَ ٱلْيَقِينِ ", "translation": "No! If you only knew with knowledge of certainty...[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَلَّا", "translit": "āَّlَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَوْ", "translit": "ْwَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَt", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عِلْمَ", "translit": "َmْlِʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْيَقِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِqَyْlٱ", "root": "يقن"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "لَتَرَوُنَّ ٱلْجَحِيمَ ", "translation": "You will surely see the Hellfire.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَتَرَوُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُwَrَtَl", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْجَحِيمَ", "translit": "َmyِḥَjgْlٱ", "root": "جحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "ثُمَّ لَتَرَوُنَّهَا عَيْنَ ٱلْيَقِينِ ", "translation": "Then you will surely see it with the eye of certainty.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَتَرَوُنَّهَا", "translit": "āَhَّnُwَrَtَl", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَʿع", "root": "عين"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْيَقِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِqَyْlٱ", "root": "يقن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "ثُمَّ لَتُسْـَٔلُنَّ يَوْمَئِذٍ عَنِ ٱلنَّعِيمِ ", "translation": "Then you will surely be asked that Day about pleasure.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَتُسْـَٔلُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُlَٔـْsُtَl", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَوْمَئِذٍ", "translit": "ٍhdِyʾَmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَنِ", "translit": "ِnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلنَّعِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِʿعَّnlٱ", "root": "نعم"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"5": [{"arabic": "ولكن للذين قد وفوا حظهم من نور اليقين فلذلك قال الله تعالى {كلا لو تعلمون علم اليقين لترون الجحيم} أي في الدنيا {ثم لترونها عين اليقين} أي في الآخرة فإذن قد ظهر أن القلب الصالح لملك الآخرة لا يكون إلا عزيزا كالشخص الصالح لملك الدنيا قسمة سادسة حاوية لمجامع النعم اعلم أن النعم تنقسم إلى ما هي غاية مطلوبة لذاتها وإلى ما هي مطلوبة لأجل", "english": "As for the first: if it is possible in existence at all, it is at the utmost extreme of remoteness. As for the second: the lower world is overflowing with it. As for the third and fourth: they exist, but at the utmost extreme of rarity. And it is inconceivable that this [rarity] should itself be rare and anomalous — rather, even with its rarity, it varies in degree of fewness and abundance. Its abundance occurs only in ages proximate to the ages of the Prophets, peace be upon them. The longer the interval [from their time] grows, the scarcer such hearts become, until the Hour draws near and God accomplishes a matter already decreed ( {وكان أمرا مفعولا} ).", "book_title": "Patience and Gratitude", "section_title_ar": "Section 994", "section_title_en": "The Division of Hearts and the Rarity of the Heart Fit for the Kingdom of the Hereafter", "section_index": 994, "anchors": "- Root: م ل ك (Malaka)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of possession, dominion, and sovereign control; al-Ayn notes the pattern shift in derived nouns.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الملك: هو المتصرف بالأمر والنهي في الجمهور\" — kingship is governance over rational beings, divided into actual sovereignty (al-tamalluk) and capacity for it (al-quwwah).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"لله الملك والملكوت\" — dominion over the visible and invisible realms. Metaphorical: \"ملك نفسه عند الغضب\" — self-mastery; here extended to the heart's sovereignty over the soul's appetites.\n- Root: ق ل ب (Qalaba)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Turning and overturning a thing from one state to another.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه\" — the heart is so named for its constant fluctuation between states.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"قلب الشيء قلبا: حوله عن وجهه.\" Metaphorical: \"رجل قلب حول: يقلب الأمور ويحتال\" — one who turns matters over; here, hearts are classified by their dominant orientation.\n- Root: ع ل م (ʿAlima)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Foundational knowing and perception.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"العلم: إدراك الشيء بحقيقته\" — apprehension of a thing's true reality, of two kinds: grasping the essence, and judging its attributes.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"هو من أعلام العلم الخافقه\" — knowledge as a raised banner. Here, \"علم اليقين\" (knowledge of certainty) vs. \"عين اليقين\" (eye of certainty) marks the literal-to-metaphorical ascent from inference to direct vision.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — The repeated use of \"إنما\" (only/indeed) throughout this passage serves to restrict predicates exclusively to their subjects, e.g., \"وإنما تكون كثرته في الأعصار القريبة\" — restricting abundance to specific eras, and \"وإنما وجب أن يكون هذا نادرا\" — restricting the cause of rarity.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Patience and Gratitude'", "badge": "Insight"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 250, 1602], [2, 1602, 2999]], "2": [[1, 350, 1370], [2, 1370, 2147], [3, 2147, 3528]], "3": [[1, 250, 1229], [2, 1229, 2039], [3, 2039, 3548]], "4": [[1, 350, 1209], [2, 1209, 2262], [3, 2262, 3134], [4, 3134, 4756]], "5": [[1, 350, 1199], [2, 1199, 1687], [3, 1687, 2994], [4, 2994, 3618], [5, 3618, 4887]], "6": [[1, 250, 2062], [2, 2062, 3600]], "7": [[1, 350, 1280], [2, 1280, 3756], [3, 3756, 4725], [4, 4725, 6428]], "8": [[1, 400, 1364], [2, 1364, 3225], [3, 3225, 4964], [4, 4964, 5562], [5, 5562, 7586]]}, "husary": {"1": [[1, 350, 2670], [2, 2670, 5067]], "2": [[1, 350, 2083], [2, 2083, 3403], [3, 3403, 5746]], "3": [[1, 350, 2162], [2, 2162, 3661], [3, 3661, 6451]], "4": [[1, 400, 2061], [2, 2061, 4096], [3, 4096, 5780], [4, 5780, 8916]], "5": [[1, 400, 1944], [2, 1944, 2832], [3, 2832, 5211], [4, 5211, 6347], [5, 6347, 8655]], "6": [[1, 350, 3268], [2, 3268, 5746]], "7": [[1, 400, 1667], [2, 1667, 5040], [3, 5040, 6361], [4, 6361, 8681]], "8": [[1, 400, 1869], [2, 1869, 4704], [3, 4704, 7352], [4, 7352, 8262], [5, 8262, 11345]]}, "minshawi": {"1": [[1, 310, 1889], [2, 1889, 3650]], "2": [[1, 160, 1428], [2, 1428, 2313], [3, 2313, 4140]], "3": [[1, 360, 1515], [2, 1515, 2299], [3, 2299, 3920]], "4": [[1, 170, 999], [2, 999, 2368], [3, 2368, 3298], [4, 3298, 5220]], "5": [[1, 340, 1434], [2, 1434, 1956], [3, 1956, 3492], [4, 3492, 4144], [5, 4144, 5820]], "6":